===Results by nation===
Spain's [[La Liga]] is the most successful national league of the competition, with eight titles won, England's [[Premier League]] are second with five titles and Brazil's [[Campeonato Brasileiro Série A|Brasileirão]] are third with four titles. Italy's [[Serie A]] and Germany's [[Bundesliga]] are fifth with two titles each. Serie A and the Bundesliga were the only undefeated national leagues which have had representatives play in the competition before the first edition with 32 teams in 2025. Argentina's [[Argentine Primera División|Primera División]] carries the dubious honour of losing the most finals without ever winning the world title, with four defeats.
